Circuits the schema itself rejects, each expecting the single code
SHAPE_INVALID.

Backend-only, and empty for a reason. Shape rejection happens at the parse
boundary rather than inside a validator, so these fixtures land with the
endpoint that maps a parse failure into the error envelope -- not with the
semantic validator in ../semantic/, which only ever sees circuits that already
parsed.

The frontend runs none of these until it gains a runtime shape validator in
Milestone 3. See ADR-0005 section 6.
